    "ImageDescription": {
      "value": "This is the transliteration of the word \"Koupalu\" in Meitei/Meetei/Manipuri script. \"Koupalu\" is an Ancient Meitei/Meetei/Manipuri name of the God who protects the North-Western direction in Meitei mythology and religion (Sanamahism/Lainingthou religion). In modern form, the word \"Koupalu\" evolved into \"Koubaru\" and then further into \"Koubru\".",
